# Cache headers (honoured by Cloudflare Pages).
# Everything Vite emits to /assets/ is content-hashed, images included, so a
# changed file always arrives under a new URL and can be cached indefinitely.
# The few files below stay in public/ at fixed paths and so need a short TTL:
# favicon.svg is fetched by path regardless of the <link> tag, and opengraph.jpg
# is referenced by absolute URL in the social meta tags, where a hashed name would
# strand links people have already shared.

# Security headers for every page and file.
# HSTS tells browsers to use HTTPS only for a year. It leaves out
# includeSubDomains, so a subdomain that ever serves plain HTTP is not locked out.
# The site is never shown inside another site's frame: X-Frame-Options for older
# browsers, and frame-ancestors, which only works as a header, not in the <meta>
# policy in index.html. This header policy sets frame-ancestors alone, so it adds
# to the <meta> policy without loosening or tightening anything else.
/*
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Content-Security-Policy: frame-ancestors 'none'

/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/favicon.svg
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=300, stale-while-revalidate=86400

/favicon.ico
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=300, stale-while-revalidate=86400

/favicon-48.png
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=300, stale-while-revalidate=86400

/favicon-192.png
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=300, stale-while-revalidate=86400

/apple-touch-icon.png
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=300, stale-while-revalidate=86400

/opengraph.jpg
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=300, stale-while-revalidate=86400
